From: djnice <djnice77@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hdmitx21: no packet writes from interrupt context while not ready

A mode setting (a playback start switching 1080p60 -> 2160p24) disables
the output (ready = 0), then enable_mode resets and reprograms the
transmitter (hdmi_hwp_init). The packet setters let a clear through
while not ready, and the Dolby Vision vsync handler clears the VSIF
right then: amdolby_vision_process -> send_hdmi_pkt ->
hdmitx_set_vsif_pkt -> hdmi_vend_infoframe_rawset -> hdmitx21_wr_reg
into the block in reset: asynchronous SError, kernel panic (Dune HD Pro
8K Plus, S928X, starting a Dolby Vision title).

Not ready, the VSIF/DRM/HDR10+ setters now leave the hardware alone when
called from interrupt context. The mode setting's own calls (process
context) are unchanged, and it sends the packets of the new mode itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hdmi_tx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hdmi_tx_main.c
@@ -886,6 +886,18 @@
 	}
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&hdev->tx_comm.edid_spinlock, flags);
 
+	/*
+	 * Not ready from interrupt context (the Dolby Vision / HDR vsync
+	 * handlers): the output is being disabled or reprogrammed by a mode
+	 * setting, which resets the transmitter. A packet write then hits a
+	 * block in reset: asynchronous SError, kernel panic. The mode setting
+	 * sends the packets of the new mode itself; a clear is only safe from
+	 * its own context.
+	 */
+	if (hdev->tx_comm.ready == 0 && in_interrupt()) {
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hdev->tx_comm.edid_spinlock, flags);
+		return;
+	}
 	/* if ready is 0, only can clear pkt */
 	if (hdev->tx_comm.ready == 0 && data) {
 		if (hdr_transfer_feature != T_BT709 ||
@@ -1240,8 +1252,13 @@
 	vsif_debug_info.type = type;
 	vsif_debug_info.tunnel_mode = tunnel_mode;
 	vsif_debug_info.signal_sdr = signal_sdr;
-	/* if ready is 0, only can clear pkt */
-	if (hdev->tx_comm.ready == 0 && type != EOTF_T_NULL) {
+	/*
+	 * if ready is 0, only can clear pkt, and not from interrupt context:
+	 * the transmitter may be in reset for a mode setting (see
+	 * hdmitx_set_drm_pkt())
+	 */
+	if (hdev->tx_comm.ready == 0 &&
+	    (type != EOTF_T_NULL || in_interrupt())) {
 		ltype = EOTF_T_NULL;
 		ltmode = -1;
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hdev->tx_comm.edid_spinlock, flags);
@@ -1582,8 +1599,8 @@
 
 	if (hdev->bist_lock)
 		return;
-	/* if ready is 0, only can clear pkt */
-	if (hdev->tx_comm.ready == 0 && data)
+	/* if ready is 0, only can clear pkt, not from interrupt context */
+	if (hdev->tx_comm.ready == 0 && (data || in_interrupt()))
 		return;
 	/* save vic to AVI when send HDR10P_VSIF */
 	if (vic == HDMI_95_3840x2160p30_16x9 ||
